    <string-array name="help_items">
        <item>Paste, type or share a link, then tap Analyze to see what the server really offers, or Download to start right away.</item>
        <item>When a link is a web page, the app lists the files it exposes (video, audio, images, documents, archives, subtitles…). Select the ones you want.</item>
        <item>Pause, resume or cancel from the Downloads tab or the notification. Resume works when the server supports HTTP range requests.</item>
        <item>Use the built-in browser for pages that need you to sign in; downloads the page starts are detected automatically.</item>
        <item>Files are saved to Downloads/UniversalDownloader unless you choose another folder in Settings.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="faq_questions">
        <item>Why does a download say resume is not supported?</item>
        <item>Why are some resources missing from a web page?</item>
        <item>Why was my download blocked?</item>
        <item>Can it download streaming video (HLS/DASH)?</item>
        <item>Where are my files?</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="faq_answers">
        <item>Some servers do not accept byte-range requests. Those files download in a single stream and restart from zero if interrupted.</item>
        <item>Only links present in the page HTML are discovered. Content created by JavaScript, behind logins or protected by DRM is not extracted.</item>
        <item>The server may require authentication (401/403), or the address may be a local/private network target, which is blocked unless allowed in Settings.</item>
        <item>No. Segmented streaming playlists are detected and reported, but only regular files are downloaded.</item>
        <item>In Downloads/UniversalDownloader, or the folder you selected in Settings &gt; Download location.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="privacy_paragraphs">
        <item>Universal Downloader does not collect, transmit or sell personal data. There are no analytics or tracking libraries in this build.</item>
        <item>The app only contacts the addresses you ask it to download from (and addresses found on those pages when you choose to download them).</item>
        <item>Download history, settings and partial files are stored privately on your device. You can clear history and temporary files, or choose not to store URLs, in Settings &gt; Privacy.</item>
        <item>Cookies are used only when you start a download from the built-in browser from a page you are signed in to. They are kept in the app’s private storage, never logged, and deleted when the download finishes.</item>
        <item>If an ad provider is added to a future build, this policy will be updated before any data is shared.</item>
    </string-array>
